Notebook[{
Cell["Lesson 08 - Projection", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"b7fd10b9-512f-4f3f-8bd5-eab10d8d71dc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Physics step.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " The flow of a coupling is the coefficient of its monomial (i",
 StyleBox["\[Nu]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ")^m (p",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ")^n in ",
 StyleBox["\[PartialD]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "s",
 StyleBox["\[CapitalGamma]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "2_ab(",
 StyleBox["\[Nu]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ", p). The module extracts it from the loop integrand: (",
 StyleBox["\[PartialD]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "/",
 StyleBox["\[PartialD]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "(i",
 StyleBox["\[Nu]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "))^m/m! at ",
 StyleBox["\[Nu]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " = 0, and the (p",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ")^n coefficient at p = 0 as the direction average of the s^{2n} Taylor \
coefficient along p = s e (",
 StyleBox["design/MOMENTUMPROJECTION.md",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ", M1, valid for any n). The external variables are set to zero first \
(\"pipeline 1\"), so the only frequency poles left are those of ",
 StyleBox["\[CapitalDelta]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["\[PlusMinus]\[Omega]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 ")."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5e3a350c-4812-424c-b024-2bf62ba1bc9d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Stage.",
